# Expo Metro Troubleshooting

## Known Issues & Fixes

### 1. `TypeError: Body is unusable: Body has already been read` on startup
**Cause**: Expo CLI's startup dependency validation makes a fetch call that fails on Node.js v22+.
**Fix**: All npm scripts must use `EXPO_NO_DEPENDENCY_VALIDATION=1` (via `cross-env`).
```json
"start": "cross-env EXPO_NO_DEPENDENCY_VALIDATION=1 expo start --port 8082"
```
> ❌ `EXPO_NO_DOCTOR=1` does NOT fix this — that flag controls a different command entirely.

### 2. `Failed to download remote update` / phone can't connect
**Root cause on this machine**: **Port 8081 is permanently held by Windows `svchost`** and cannot be freed.
Metro defaults to 8081, conflicts with svchost, and enters a broken state.
**Fix**: Always use `--port 8082` (or any port other than 8081) in all expo start scripts.

### 3. Metro stuck / terminal freezes / 96% CPU node process
**Cause**: Stale Node.js processes from previous broken Metro sessions pile up.
**Diagnosis & fix steps**:
```powershell
# 1. Kill all node processes
Get-Process -Name "node" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force

# 2. Verify port 8081 blocker (svchost - do NOT try to kill it)
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 8081 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

# 3. Confirm target port is free
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 8082 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

# 4. Clear Metro temp cache
Get-ChildItem $env:TEMP -Filter "metro-*" | Remove-Item -Recurse -Force
Get-ChildItem $env:TEMP -Filter "haste-*" | Remove-Item -Recurse -Force

# 5. Start on free port
npm run start
```

## Correct npm scripts (package.json)
```json
"start": "cross-env EXPO_NO_DEPENDENCY_VALIDATION=1 expo start --port 8082",
"dev":   "cross-env EXPO_NO_DEPENDENCY_VALIDATION=1 expo start -c --port 8082"
```

## Node.js Version
This project runs on **Node.js v24.13.1** (managed via nvm).
After any `nvm use` version switch, always run `npm install` to recompile native bindings.
